---
layout: changelog
title: Deploy server-rendered sites from npm, pnpm, and Bun workspaces
date: 2026-11-10
cover: /images/blog/announcing-monorepo-support-for-sites/cover.avif
tags: sites
---

Appwrite Sites now deploys server-rendered apps straight from a monorepo. Set the root directory to `./` and build only your app, for example with `pnpm --filter web build`. Then set the output directory to the app's build output from the repo root, such as `./apps/web/.next`.

- Works with npm, pnpm, and Bun workspaces.
- Works with every JavaScript SSR framework: Next.js, Nuxt, Astro, SvelteKit, Remix, TanStack Start, Angular, and Analog.
- Appwrite copies in the workspace packages your app uses and leaves your other apps out of the deployment.
- Next.js standalone output works in a monorepo too.
- Nuxt and Remix apps installed with pnpm now deploy correctly in single-app repos as well.

On self-hosted Appwrite, pull the latest image for your build runtime, such as `openruntimes/node:v5-22`, and redeploy.

